From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: give the dcp and the display subsystem a phandle

dtc writes a phandle only for a node some property references. Nothing
references &dcp or &display_subsystem (the J716s DT only extends them), so
the DTB has no phandle on either, while a loader that edits them (m1n1's
T6050 display hand-off re-finds each node it edits by phandle, because
every property it adds moves the offsets after it) needs one. Write the
phandles by hand: dtc keeps an explicit phandle and numbers the generated
ones around it.

Not applied. The loader fix (m1n1 gives a node without a phandle one) is
the proper one; this is only for a loader that has not got it.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
@@ -829,6 +829,9 @@
 
 	dcp: dcp@48ae00000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t6050-dcp", "apple,dcp";
+		/* nothing references this node, so dtc would give it no phandle; a loader that edits it
+		 * (m1n1's T6050 display hand-off) finds it again by phandle */
+		phandle = <0x74>;
 		reg = <0x4 0x8ae00000 0x0 0x4000>,
 		      <0x4 0x88000000 0x0 0x4000000>,
 		      <0x4 0x8a240000 0x0 0x10000>,
@@ -1105,6 +1108,8 @@
 / {
 	display_subsystem: display-subsystem {
 		compatible = "apple,display-subsystem";
+		/* as for the dcp: nothing references this node */
+		phandle = <0x75>;
 		iommus = <&dart_disp0 0>;
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
